#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/2
msgid ""
"I admit, human thought may not be fully compatible\n"
"with level-headed decision making.\n"
msgstr ""
"我承认，人类思维未必\n"
"完全适合理性决策。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/3
msgid ""
"Then again, is there such a thing as non-human\n"
"thought?\n"
msgstr ""
"话说回来，\n"
"真有非人类的思维吗？\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/4
msgid ""
"The moment computers became so advanced\n"
msgstr ""
"当计算机已经先进到\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/5
msgid ""
"that they could calculate faster than human\n"
"beings, a new dream was born.\n"
msgstr ""
"计算速度超过人类，\n"
"一个新的梦想就诞生了。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/6
msgid ""
"Dream?\n"
msgstr ""
"梦想？\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/7
msgid ""
"If we can create a machine that can do advanced\n"
"mathematics,\n"
msgstr ""
"既然能造出会做\n"
"高等数学的机器，\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/8
msgid ""
"why can't we create one that can think like a\n"
"human?\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么不能造出\n"
"像人一样思考的机器？\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/9
msgid ""
"The 19th century author Auguste Villiers\n"
"l'Isle-Adam wrote a book called \"Tomorrow's Eve\"\n"
msgstr ""
"19世纪作家维利耶·德·利尔-亚当\n"
"写过一本《未来的夏娃》，\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/10
msgid ""
"in which the protagonist fashions an artificial\n"
"woman to serve as his ideal lover...\n"
msgstr ""
"主人公造出一个机械女人，\n"
"当作理想的恋人……\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/11
msgid ""
"I believe the idea of creating an intelligent being\n"
"with our own hands\n"
msgstr ""
"我认为，亲手创造智能生命\n"
"这个念头，\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/12
msgid ""
"is one of mankind's oldest dreams.\n"
msgstr ""
"是人类最古老的梦想之一。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/13
msgid ""
"So AI is a product of people's dreams then.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说AI是梦想的产物。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/14
msgid ""
"Not only AI. Civilization itself\n"
msgstr ""
"不只是AI。文明本身\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/15
msgid ""
"is the process by which mankind gives form to its\n"
"dreams.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是人类\n"
"把梦想具象化的过程。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/16
msgid ""
"But not all dreams are pleasant.\n"
msgstr ""
"但并非所有梦想都美好。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/17
msgid ""
"Some have expressed fears about \"non-human\n"
"intelligence.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"有人表达了对「非人类智能」\n"
"的担忧。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/18
msgid ""
"Yeah, they want the benefits with none of the risks.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，只想得好处不想担风险。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/19
msgid ""
"Some fear that intelligent robots might rise up and\n"
"rebel against their human masters,\n"
msgstr ""
"有人担心智能机器人会起身\n"
"反抗人类主人，\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/20
msgid ""
"as portrayed by the Czech writer Karel Capek in\n"
"his \"Rossum's Universal Robots.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"正如捷克作家恰佩克\n"
"在《罗素姆万能机器人》里写的。\n"

#: codec/1/221/0xdda20/21
msgid ""
"Or in the 1970 film \"Colossus: The Forbin Project,\"\n"
msgstr ""
"还有1970年的电影《巨人：福宾计划》，\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/0
msgid ""
"So what's an 'expert system?'\n"
msgstr ""
"啥是“专家系统”？\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/1
msgid ""
"The AI housed within Peace Walker began\n"
"development as such a system.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者搭载的AI最初就是作为\n"
"这种系统开发的。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/2
msgid ""
"An expert system is a type of proxy program\n"
msgstr ""
"专家系统是一种代理程序，\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/3
msgid ""
"by which a computer makes decisions as an expert\n"
"would.\n"
msgstr ""
"by which a computer makes decisions as an expert\n"
"would.\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/4
msgid ""
"The program \"MYCIN,\" for example,\n"
msgstr ""
"比如“MYCIN”程序，\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/5
msgid ""
"is a system that decides which kinds of antibiotics\n"
"to prescribe.\n"
msgstr ""
"is a system that decides which kinds of antibiotics\n"
"to prescribe.\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/6
msgid ""
"The system asks the patient a series of questions\n"
msgstr ""
"系统会向病人问一系列问题，\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/7
msgid ""
"to narrow down the range of appropriate drugs.\n"
msgstr ""
"以缩小适用药物的范围。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/8
msgid ""
"So you programmed Peace Walker to prescribe live\n"
"nuclear warheads instead of penicillin.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你把和平行者编成开核弹头\n"
"而不是青霉素。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/9
msgid ""
"What I realized, however, was that a simple expert\n"
"system wasn't up to the task.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我意识到，单纯的专家系统\n"
"无法胜任。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/10
msgid ""
"You need more than expertise to launch a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""
"发射核弹光靠专业知识不够。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/11
msgid ""
"Indeed. Expertise is a necessary prerequisite but\n"
"insufficient on its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。专业知识是必要前提，\n"
"但本身不够。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/12
msgid ""
"Deciding to launch a retaliatory strike requires\n"
"consideration of a wider range of factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"决定发动报复性打击需要\n"
"考虑更广泛的因素。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/13
msgid ""
"In such a scenario, the entire global situation\n"
"becomes the criterion for making a decision.\n"
msgstr ""
"这种情况下，全球局势\n"
"本身就是决策标准。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/14
msgid ""
"Makes sense. You screw up the prescription, and\n"
"the whole world goes into anaphylactic shock.\n"
msgstr ""
"有道理。你开错药，\n"
"全世界都会过敏性休克。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/15
msgid ""
"A \"weak AI\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“弱AI”\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/16
msgid ""
"that has only a limited range of knowledge upon\n"
"which to base its decisions won't cut it.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有有限知识作为决策依据，\n"
"是不够的。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/17
msgid ""
"Therefore, I had the AI study The Boss' thought\n"
"patterns,\n"
msgstr ""
"因此，我让AI学习了THE BOSS的\n"
"思维模式，\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/18
msgid ""
"thus creating a true expert system - a \"strong AI.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"从而造出真正专家系统，即“强AI”。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/19
msgid ""
"You couldn't leave the world in the hands of\n"
"something\n"
msgstr ""
"你不能把世界交到\n"
"某种东西手里\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/20
msgid ""
"with anything less than an absolute worldview.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有绝对世界观的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/21
msgid ""
"I could have built a simple expert system in no\n"
"time at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"我本可以很快造出\n"
"简单的专家系统。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/22
msgid ""
"Say, how would you like a system that decides\n"
"which guns you should equip\n"
msgstr ""
"想不想要套系统，按任务参数\n"
"决定你带什么枪？\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/23
msgid ""
"according to the mission's parameters?\n"
msgstr ""
"免了。我可不想把命交给别人的判断。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/24
msgid ""
"I'll pass. I'm not gonna leave my life up to\n"
"somebody else's judgment.\n"
msgstr ""
"我拒绝。我不会把自己的人生交给\n"
"别人的判断。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/25
msgid ""
"Especially not a machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"相反的方向……什么意思？\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xdeeb0/0
msgid ""
"With current technology, AI are inevitably enormous\n"
"in size.\n"
msgstr ""
"以现在的技术，\n"
"AI的体积必然庞大。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xdeeb0/1
msgid ""
"But as circuit integration continues to advance,\n"
"they'll become even smaller.\n"
msgstr ""
"但随着集成电路不断进步，\n"
"它们会越来越小。\n"

#: codec/1/222/0xdeeb0/2
msgid ""
"As small as human brains, and perhaps smaller\n"
"than that.\n"
msgstr ""
"小到人脑那么大，\n"
"甚至可能更小。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 473..1462
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/0
msgid ""
"The opposite direction... What does that mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"越来越多的AI正变成专精大规模信息处理的系统，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 1490..3092
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/1
msgid ""
"More and more AI are becoming systems that\n"
"specialize in mass information processing\n"
msgstr ""
"越来越多的AI正在成为专门\n"
"处理海量信息的系统\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 3176..4304
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/2
msgid ""
"- without human intelligence, thought, or emotion.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种没有个性、没有自我的机器，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 4388..5349
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/3
msgid ""
"A machine that has no individualism or sense of\n"
"self,\n"
msgstr ""
"一台没有个体意识或自我\n"
"意识的机器，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 5461..7077
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/4
msgid ""
"but rather behaves as a collective, exhibiting the\n"
"qualities of a society.\n"
msgstr ""
"而是作为一个集体运作，展现出\n"
"社会的特质。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 7091..7453
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/5
msgid ""
"Like a beehive?\n"
msgstr ""
"像蜂巢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 7509..9557
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/6
msgid ""
"Yes. It aggregates data collected by individuals and\n"
"determines how the collective will act\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。它汇总个体收集的数据，并\n"
"决定集体将如何行动\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 9613..10685
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/7
msgid ""
"just as honeybees travel between the hive and\n"
"flowers.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像蜜蜂在蜂巢与\n"
"花朵之间往返。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 10769..11939
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/8
msgid ""
"The key to achieving that will be networking AI\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""
"实现这目标的关键是把AI\n"
"连成网络。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 11995..13193
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/9
msgid ""
"I don't know how to say this, but... that kind of\n"
"gives me the creeps.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道该怎么说，但……那种\n"
"让我毛骨悚然。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 13221..14586
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/10
msgid ""
"But if your goal is to control society, it's the better\n"
"model to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"但若目标是控制社会，那它是更\n"
"好用的模型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 14642..16133
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/11
msgid ""
"It lets you filter data - disseminate only what you\n"
"want disseminated.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能让你筛选数据——只传播你\n"
"想传播的内容。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 16202..17707
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/12
msgid ""
"Of course, I myself have no interest in an AI\n"
"without a shred of life to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，我本人对一个毫无\n"
"生命气息的AI没有兴趣。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 473..2452
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/0
msgid ""
"Earlier, you called the Mammal Pod a butterfly. Not\n"
"a pupa or a cocoon, but an imago.\n"
msgstr ""
"之前你称哺乳动物舱为蝴蝶。不是\n"
"蛹，不是茧，是成虫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 2507..3873
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/1
msgid ""
"Yes. The AI that came before the Mammal Pod\n"
"were works in progress.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。哺乳动物舱之前的AI\n"
"都是未完成的作品。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 3928..4332
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/2
msgid ""
"Works in progress?\n"
msgstr ""
"它们足以维持机体运转。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 4346..4931
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/3
msgid ""
"They were enough to keep the frame running.\n"
msgstr ""
"但不足以决定核报复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 4931..6018
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/4
msgid ""
"But not enough to make decisions about nuclear\n"
"retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""
"但还不足以做出核\n"
"报复的决定。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 6060..6965
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/5
msgid ""
"They weren't quite complete. They were pupae.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们还不完整，是蛹。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 7035..8359
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/6
msgid ""
"Only when I added The Boss' data did the AI take\n"
"on its true form,\n"
msgstr ""
"只有加入The Boss数据后，AI才\n"
"显出真身，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 8512..9376
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/7
msgid ""
"becoming a butterfly and taking flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"化蝶起飞。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 9404..10448
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/8
msgid ""
"And that's why the nose art on Peace Walker was\n"
"a butterfly...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以和平行者机头的图案才是\n"
"蝴蝶……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 10476..11730
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/9
msgid ""
"I gave the Mammal AI the code name \"BS-Imago.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我给哺乳AI起代号“BS-Imago”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 11828..12705
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/10
msgid ""
"\"BS\" is short for Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"“BS”是BOSS的缩写。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/0
msgid ""
"Huey called that gigantic unmanned chopper a\n"
"Chrysalis.\n"
msgstr ""
"休伊把那架巨型无人直升机\n"
"叫做「蛹」。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/1
msgid ""
"Is that another one of your AI code names?\n"
msgstr ""
"那也是你们AI的代号？\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/2
msgid ""
"Yes. You're referring to the TJ-Chrysalis 6000.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，你说的是TJ-Chrysalis 6000。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/3
msgid ""
"There's also the GW-Pupa 5000, the TR-Cocoon\n"
"7000...\n"
msgstr ""
"还有GW-Pupa 5000、\n"
"TR-Cocoon 7000……\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/4
msgid ""
"I get it. A hovercraft type and a treaded type....\n"
msgstr ""
"我明白了。气垫型和履带型……\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/5
msgid ""
"And those letters on the front, TJ and GW or\n"
"whatever, those are initials?\n"
msgstr ""
"前面那些字母，TJ、GW什么的，\n"
"是名字的首字母？\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/6
msgid ""
"Correct. The initials of the American Presidents\n"
"whose faces are carved\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。是那些被刻在山上\n"
"的美国总统名字的缩写，\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/7
msgid ""
"into Mount Rushmore.\n"
msgstr ""
"刻在拉什莫尔山上的。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/8
msgid ""
"Then you're missing one.\n"
msgstr ""
"那你们少了一个。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/9
msgid ""
"I assigned that one to the Reptile Pod. AL-Aurelia\n"
"8000.\n"
msgstr ""
"我把那个用在了爬行动物舱：\n"
"AL-Aurelia 8000。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/10
msgid ""
"Aurelia... another word for chrysalis... a pupa just\n"
"before it emerges.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aurelia……也就是「蛹」的别称，\n"
"指羽化前的虫蛹。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/11
msgid ""
"All of the initials except for \"BS\" were of Coldman's\n"
"choosing.\n"
msgstr ""
"除了「BS」，\n"
"其他缩写都是科尔德曼选的。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/12
msgid ""
"I chose mine from the storied ranks of British\n"
"royalty.\n"
msgstr ""
"我则是从英国王室\n"
"的历代君主里挑的。\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/13
msgid ""
"MS, AV, EW...\n"
msgstr ""
"MS、AV、EW……\n"

#: codec/1/223/0xdfc70/14
msgid ""
"...What do those stand for.\n"
msgstr ""
"……这些是哪几个？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 571..1267
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/0
msgid ""
"What did you mean by \"the Ghost in the Machine\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你说的“机器中的幽灵”啥意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 1281..2633
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/1
msgid ""
"Oh, that... It's a term coined by the philosopher\n"
"Gilbert Ryle.\n"
msgstr ""
"那个啊……哲学家\n"
"吉尔伯特·赖尔提出的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 2661..3232
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/2
msgid ""
"You've heard of Descartes, yes?\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道笛卡尔吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 3260..3817
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/3
msgid ""
"\"I think, therefore I am...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“我思故我在……”\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 3845..5419
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/4
msgid ""
"That is the one. Descartes espoused the dualistic\n"
"theory of mind and body.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是他。笛卡尔主张\n"
"心物二元论。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 5433..6715
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/5
msgid ""
"He believed that our thinking minds exist in a\n"
"separate dimension from our bodies,\n"
msgstr ""
"他认为思考的心灵存在于\n"
"与肉体不同的维度，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7397
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/6
msgid ""
"which are governed by the laws of physics.\n"
msgstr ""
"而肉体受物理法则支配。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 7467..9041
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/7
msgid ""
"But if that were true, then couldn't you say that a\n"
"mechanical \"body\"\n"
msgstr ""
"若真如此，那被幽灵“心灵”\n"
"寄居的机械“肉体”，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 9125..10337
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/8
msgid ""
"inhabited by a ghost \"mind\" is a human being?\n"
msgstr ""
"岂不也能算是人？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11340
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/9
msgid ""
"Ryle criticized Descartes on those grounds,\n"
msgstr ""
"赖尔正是以此批判笛卡尔，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 11340..12469
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/10
msgid ""
"saying such a thing surely wouldn't be human.\n"
msgstr ""
"说那种东西绝不可能是人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 12469..12817
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/11
msgid ""
"Why'd you bring it up?\n"
msgstr ""
"你提这干嘛？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 12845..13848
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/12
msgid ""
"I wasn't thinking of Ryle in particular when I said it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我说的时候并没特意想到赖尔。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 13904..15450
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/13
msgid ""
"I simply thought that if a person is composed of a\n"
"machine and a ghost,\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是想，若人由\n"
"机械与幽灵构成，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 15575..16272
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/14
msgid ""
"perhaps the opposite is true as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"或许反过来也成立。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 16342..18752
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/15
msgid ""
"Perhaps by placing a ghost inside a machine, we\n"
"could in effect give birth to a new person.\n"
msgstr ""
"把幽灵放进机械里，或许就能\n"
"造出新的生命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 18780..19462
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/16
msgid ""
"And that was your idea for the Boss AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是你造BOSS AI的构想？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 19490..20953
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/17
msgid ""
"The moment you ripped the memory board out, the\n"
"Mammal Pod ceased to function.\n"
msgstr ""
"你拔出存储板那一刻，\n"
"哺乳舱就停止运转了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 21023..21441
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/18
msgid ""
"It should have been dead.\n"
msgstr ""
"它本该已经死了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 21524..23252
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/19
msgid ""
"And yet Peace Walker righted itself, singing a song\n"
"of peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"可和平行者却自己站起，\n"
"唱起和平之歌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 23294..25161
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/20
msgid ""
"I couldn't help but feel... that her soul had come to\n"
"inhabit Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不禁觉得……她的灵魂\n"
"寄居到了和平行者里。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/0
msgid ""
"Are you familiar with the film \"2001: A Space\n"
"Odyssey\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你看过电影《2001太空\n"
"漫游》吗？\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/1
msgid ""
"I've heard of it, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"听说过，但……\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/2
msgid ""
"Of course not. I didn't expect you to be cultured\n"
"enough to appreciate such things.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然没有。我也没指望你有文化\n"
"到能欣赏这种东西。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, thanks. Anyway...\n"
msgstr ""
"谢了。总之……\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/4
msgid ""
"\"2001\" features an AI called HAL,\n"
msgstr ""
"《2001》里有个AI叫HAL，\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/5
msgid ""
"a highly advanced system that controls an\n"
"exploration spacecraft.\n"
msgstr ""
"是个控制探索飞船的\n"
"高度先进系统。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/6
msgid ""
"It can converse with people, and even play chess.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能跟人对话，甚至下棋。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/7
msgid ""
"Huh. Now where have I heard that before...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。这话我在哪儿听过……\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/8
msgid ""
"The way HAL was portrayed was truly superb.\n"
msgstr ""
"HAL的刻画真是绝了。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/10
msgid ""
"HAL is given secret orders that not even the\n"
"ship's captain knows about.\n"
msgstr ""
"HAL接到了连船长\n"
"都不知道的密令。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/11
msgid ""
"Naturally, he's not allowed to divulge them to the\n"
"crew. The stress of it causes HAL to crack.\n"
msgstr ""
"它自然不能向船员泄露。\n"
"这种压力让它崩溃了。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/12
msgid ""
"Crack?\n"
msgstr ""
"崩溃？\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/13
msgid ""
"Go crazy. Though there are those who interpret it\n"
"differently.\n"
msgstr ""
"发疯。不过也有人\n"
"有别的解读。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/14
msgid ""
"One by one, HAL kills off the crew until the captain\n"
"finally shuts it down...\n"
msgstr ""
"HAL一个个杀掉船员，直到船长\n"
"最终把它关掉……\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/15
msgid ""
"The film offers amazing insights into AI - their\n"
"growth, their utility, their faults - and their fear of\n"
"death.\n"
msgstr ""
"这部电影对AI见解惊人，它们的\n"
"成长、功用、缺陷，以及对\n"
"死亡的恐惧。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/16
msgid ""
"You must have found it useful in your research,\n"
"then.\n"
msgstr ""
"那你研究中一定觉得它有用\n"
"吧。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/17
msgid ""
"Must you always be so... utilitarian?\n"
msgstr ""
"你就非得这么……功利吗？\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/18
msgid ""
"It doesn't matter whether or not it's useful. What\n"
"matters is that it inspired me.\n"
msgstr ""
"有没有用不重要。重要的是\n"
"它启发了我。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/19
msgid ""
"Then it was USEFUL.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是有用。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/20
msgid ""
"Never mind. The portrayal of HAL wasn't the only\n"
"wonderful thing about the film.\n"
msgstr ""
"算了。HAL的刻画并不是\n"
"这片子唯一精彩之处。\n"

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/21
msgid ""
"It was full of hints about the future of human\n"
"evolution. Truly a film for the ages.\n"
msgstr ""
"它充满了对人类进化未来的暗示。\n"
"真是传世之作。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/0
msgid ""
"Strangelove, when did you and The Boss first\n"
"meet?\n"
msgstr ""
"斯特兰奇洛夫，你和THE BOSS\n"
"最初是怎么认识的？\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/1
msgid ""
"...Did she ever tell you about what she saw in\n"
"space?\n"
msgstr ""
"……她跟你讲过她在太空\n"
"看到啥了吗？\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/3
msgid ""
"I saw the same thing along with her.\n"
msgstr ""
"我和她看到一样的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/4
msgid ""
"The Soviets beat America into space with Sputnik,\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联用斯普特尼克抢先进入太空，\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/5
msgid ""
"and so America rushed to be first in manned\n"
"spaceflight.\n"
msgstr ""
"于是美国急着争当\n"
"载人航天第一。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/6
msgid ""
"NASA used her as their top-secret guinea pig,\n"
"launching her deep into the cold blackness of\n"
"space.\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA将她用作绝密实验豚鼠，\n"
"把她发射到寒冷漆黑的\n"
"太空中。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/7
msgid ""
"I took part in the project. As a scientist.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以科学家身份参与了计划。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/8
msgid ""
"You were there with her...?\n"
msgstr ""
"你和她一起在那里……？\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/9
msgid ""
"Yes... For a brief time, we were one and the same,\n"
"she and I.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的……有段时间，她和我\n"
"如同一体。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/10
msgid ""
"We sought each other out... Completed each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们彼此寻找……彼此补全。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/11
msgid ""
"Did you know that inside every woman there's a\n"
"universe,\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道每个女人体内都有一个\n"
"宇宙吗，\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/12
msgid ""
"and that we are able to sense this in each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"而我们能互相感知到它。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/13
msgid ""
"We connected because of our empathetic female\n"
"brains.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们因女性同理心\n"
"大脑而相通。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/14
msgid ""
"As time went on... I began to have doubts about\n"
"offering such a noble soul as sacrifice.\n"
msgstr ""
"随着时间推移……我开始怀疑，\n"
"是否该牺牲如此高贵的灵魂。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/15
msgid ""
"Why would they...? Why did she have to...?\n"
msgstr ""
"他们为什么要……？她为何非得……？\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/16
msgid ""
"...The flight test was a narrow success, and she\n"
"miraculously made it back alive.\n"
msgstr ""
"……飞行试验勉强成功，她\n"
"奇迹般活着回来了。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/17
msgid ""
"But her mind and body were horribly mangled, and\n"
"there was nothing I could do for her.\n"
msgstr ""
"但她的身心已支离破碎，\n"
"我无能为力。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/18
msgid ""
"We were no longer one and the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不再是一体了。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/19
msgid ""
"She went away, and I, having nothing else to live\n"
"for, immersed myself in AI research.\n"
msgstr ""
"她走了，我别无寄托，\n"
"便投身于AI研究。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/20
msgid ""
"Hoping that no one would ever have to make her\n"
"sacrifice again.\n"
msgstr ""
"只盼再无人需要像她那样\n"
"牺牲。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/21
msgid ""
"I never knew...\n"
msgstr ""
"我从未知道……\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/22
msgid ""
"It's not really worth knowing.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道也罢。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/23
msgid ""
"We were ships passing in the night, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们只是夜里擦肩而过的船。\n"

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/24
msgid ""
"Perhaps someday I'll tell you the long version, if\n"
"you're interested.\n"
msgstr ""
"若你有兴趣，改天我讲\n"
"详细版。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 445..1448
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/0
msgid ""
"That was quite a warm welcome you gave me at\n"
"the base in Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"你在哥斯达黎加基地\n"
"可真够热情地迎接我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 1476..2465
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/1
msgid ""
"...Sorry about that. But I simply had to know.\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉。但我必须弄清楚。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 2493..2953
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/2
msgid ""
"The Boss' final act?\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS最后的行动？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 2981..4778
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/3
msgid ""
"Yes. By inputting her thoughts and actions into the\n"
"AI, I was imbuing it with her mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。把她的思想与行动输入AI，\n"
"便是将她的心智注入其中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 4848..5921
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/4
msgid ""
"The only thing I couldn't understand was her final\n"
"act.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯独她最后的行动，\n"
"我无法理解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 5935..6450
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/5
msgid ""
"Operation Snake Eater...\n"
msgstr ""
"食蛇者行动……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 6478..8874
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/6
msgid ""
"Official history says she betrayed her homeland\n"
"and defected to the enemy... and was killed by you.\n"
msgstr ""
"官方说法是她背叛祖国\n"
"投敌……然后被你杀死。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 8944..10644
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/7
msgid ""
"...But it didn't make sense. The Boss would be the\n"
"last person on earth to betray her country.\n"
msgstr ""
"……但这说不通。THE BOSS\n"
"绝不可能背叛自己的国家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 10699..11326
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/8
msgid ""
"It was logically inconsistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"逻辑上自相矛盾。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 11368..11744
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/9
msgid ""
"...It was, wasn't it?\n"
msgstr ""
"……没错吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 11772..13096
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/10
msgid ""
"That internal inconsistency prevented the AI from\n"
"activating properly -\n"
msgstr ""
"这种内部矛盾让AI无法\n"
"正常启动——\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 13151..13862
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/11
msgid ""
"just as HAL malfunctioned in the film.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像电影里HAL出故障一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 13904..14907
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/12
msgid ""
"I understood the reasoning. But I had to have\n"
"proof.\n"
msgstr ""
"我理解这个推理。但我需要\n"
"证据。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 15004..16495
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/13
msgid ""
"Proof of her final act. Her true intentions. One way\n"
"or another!\n"
msgstr ""
"她最后行动的证明。她真正的意图。无论如何\n"
"都要找到！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 16509..17233
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/14
msgid ""
"So you tried to squeeze it out of me, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你想逼我说出来？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 17247..19560
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/15
msgid ""
"As a matter of fact, I did. Your silence was the\n"
"very answer I was looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。你的沉默正是\n"
"我要找的答案。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 459..1156
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/0
msgid ""
"What did you think of Peace Walker's final act?\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么看和平行者的最后行动？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 1170..2089
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/1
msgid ""
"I recreated her thought patterns exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"我精确复现了她的思维模式。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 2159..2800
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/2
msgid ""
"It was exactly what she would have done.\n"
msgstr ""
"那正是她会做的事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 2883..4249
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/3
msgid ""
"The world's most empathetic mind weighed the\n"
"past, the future,\n"
msgstr ""
"世界上最富共情的心智权衡了\n"
"过去、未来，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 4304..5544
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/4
msgid ""
"and the entire world... and decided not to retaliate.\n"
msgstr ""
"以及整个世界……决定不予报复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 5670..6339
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/5
msgid ""
"Merely knowing that is enough for me.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道这点，我就够了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 6436..7801
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/6
msgid ""
"...So what you're saying is, we don't need\n"
"deterrence to have peace?\n"
msgstr ""
"……所以你是说，我们不需要\n"
"威慑也能有和平？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 7815..9278
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/7
msgid ""
"I didn't say that. What's important is that we wish\n"
"for peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没那么说。重要的是我们\n"
"渴望和平。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 9320..10532
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/8
msgid ""
"MSF needs a way to protect itself from the might\n"
"of nations.\n"
msgstr ""
"MSF需要保护自己免受\n"
"各国武力威胁的手段。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 10588..11661
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/9
msgid ""
"Survival requires pragmatic thought and action.\n"
msgstr ""
"生存需要务实的思想和行动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 11758..12552
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/10
msgid ""
"But, you still must retain your ideals.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你必须始终坚守理想。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 12705..14224
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/11
msgid ""
"If the gap between reality and those ideals ever\n"
"leads you to lose them...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果现实与理想的差距\n"
"让你失去了理想……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 14363..15088
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/12
msgid ""
"I doubt MSF will survive.\n"
msgstr ""
"MSF恐怕无法存续。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/0
msgid ""
"Strangelove... Is that a code name?\n"
msgstr ""
"奇爱博士……是代号吗？\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/1
msgid ""
"No, just a nickname.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，只是个外号。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/2
msgid ""
"Don't tell me you don't recognize it! From Kubrick's\n"
"\"Dr. Strangelove, or How I Learned to Stop\n"
"Worrying and Love the Bomb?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"你别告诉我你没认出来！\n"
"库布里克的《奇爱博士：\n"
"我如何学会停止恐惧并爱上炸弹》？\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/3
msgid ""
"It's a film that came out in 1964... a dark comedy\n"
"about the absurdity of nuclear deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是1964年的电影……一部\n"
"讽刺核威慑荒谬性的黑色喜剧。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/4
msgid ""
"You were in a movie?\n"
msgstr ""
"你上过电影？\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/5
msgid ""
"No, stupid! I got my nickname because of that\n"
"movie.\n"
msgstr ""
"笨蛋，不是！\n"
"这个外号就是因那部电影来的。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/6
msgid ""
"Why, because you look like the doctor in the movie?\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你长得像电影里的博士？\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/7
msgid ""
"...No. That Dr. Strangelove was a man.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不是。那个奇爱博士是男的。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/8
msgid ""
"So...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以……\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/9
msgid ""
"Back when I was at ARPA (Advanced Research\n"
"Projects Agency),\n"
msgstr ""
"当年我在ARPA（\n"
"高级研究计划局）的时候，\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/10
msgid ""
"I kept a photo of The Boss on my desk.\n"
msgstr ""
"桌上摆着一张The Boss的照片。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/11
msgid ""
"I was totally engrossed in my research and showed\n"
"no interest in the opposite sex,\n"
msgstr ""
"我一心扑在研究上，\n"
"对异性毫无兴趣，\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/12
msgid ""
"plus I had a photo of a woman on my desk...\n"
msgstr ""
"桌上又摆着一个女人的照片……\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/13
msgid ""
"The fools around me turned it into a cruel taunt,\n"
"calling me \"Strangelove.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"周围的蠢货就以此嘲弄我，\n"
"叫我「奇爱博士」。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/14
msgid ""
"Even for a bunch of shut-ins who never went out\n"
"to the cinema, that title seemed to ring true with\n"
"them.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪怕他们是一群从不出门\n"
"看电影的宅人，\n"
"这个片名也让他们觉得贴切。\n"

#: codec/1/226/0xe2bb0/15
msgid ""
"Anyhow, in their eyes homosexuality was something\n"
"strange.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之在他们眼里，\n"
"同性恋就是「奇怪」的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 487..1407
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/0
msgid ""
"So you were with ARPA before you came here,\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"你来这里之前是在ARPA工作，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 1476..3037
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/1
msgid ""
"Yes. Back then it was really the only place I could\n"
"make a living from my AI research.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。那时那是我唯一能靠\n"
"AI研究谋生的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 3120..3413
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/2
msgid ""
"And before that?\n"
msgstr ""
"那之前呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 3441..4388
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/3
msgid ""
"I started out at NASA. That's where I met her.\n"
msgstr ""
"我最早在NASA，就在那遇见她。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 4416..4890
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/4
msgid ""
"When Boss went into space...\n"
msgstr ""
"BOSS上太空时……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 4917..6339
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/5
msgid ""
"...Yes. It was that incident that turned me away\n"
"from aerospace engineering.\n"
msgstr ""
"……对。正是那次事故让我离开了\n"
"航天工程。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 6422..7397
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/6
msgid ""
"Space is entirely too hazardous a place for human\n"
"beings.\n"
msgstr ""
"太空对人类\n"
"太危险了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 7467..8373
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/7
msgid ""
"That was why I felt an immediate need to develop\n"
"AI.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是为什么我感到迫切需要开发\n"
"AI。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 8442..10267
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/8
msgid ""
"As it turned out, rockets later became much safer,\n"
"and mankind reached the surface of the moon...\n"
msgstr ""
"后来火箭安全多了，\n"
"人类也登上了月球……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 10351..11466
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/9
msgid ""
"In any event, it was a hollow Cold War victory.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，那只是冷战的空洞胜利。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 11563..13096
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/10
msgid ""
"When you get down to it, a nuclear missile is just a\n"
"rocket with a nuclear warhead strapped to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"说到底，核导弹不过是绑了核弹头的\n"
"火箭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 13165..14698
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/11
msgid ""
"Thus, taking the initiative in the space race was\n"
"tantamount to a military show of force.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以太空竞赛抢先就等于\n"
"军事示威。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 14795..16021
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/12
msgid ""
"But the budgetary strain was too big for\n"
"Washington or Moscow to handle.\n"
msgstr ""
"但预算压力太大，华盛顿或莫斯科都\n"
"无法承受。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 16021..17916
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/13
msgid ""
"Yes, and then there was the Cuban Missile Crisis\n"
"and the Vietnam War. And then came Détente...\n"
msgstr ""
"对，接着是古巴导弹危机和越南战争，\n"
"然后是缓和……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 17986..20020
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/14
msgid ""
"Having leapt ahead of the Soviet Union with its\n"
"moon landing, America shut down the Apollo\n"
"program in '72.\n"
msgstr ""
"凭借登月领先于苏联后，美国于72年\n"
"关闭了阿波罗\n"
"计划。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 20075..22068
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/15
msgid ""
"It was around then that ARPA was downsized and\n"
"renamed DARPA, the \"D\" standing for \"defense.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"差不多那时ARPA缩编改名DARPA，\n"
"那个D就是防务。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 22151..24144
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/16
msgid ""
"With few prospects for continuing my AI research,\n"
"Coldman's invitation was a godsend.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的AI研究前途渺茫，\n"
"科尔德曼的邀请是天赐良机。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 24325..25370
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/17
msgid ""
"It was also a chance to have them collect data on\n"
"her.\n"
msgstr ""
"也是让他们收集她数据的\n"
"机会。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 25397..25955
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/18
msgid ""
"The end result being this mess.\n"
msgstr ""
"结果就成了这烂摊子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 25969..27557
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/19
msgid ""
"But we did learn something valuable from her - the\n"
"nobility of peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我们从她身上学到宝贵东西，\n"
"和平的崇高。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/0
msgid ""
"Why'd you agree to come here - to Mother Base?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为什么答应来母基地？\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/1
msgid ""
"You intrigued me.\n"
msgstr ""
"你让我感兴趣。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/2
msgid ""
"Me? ...Hold on, you're not planning on modeling\n"
"your next AI after me...\n"
msgstr ""
"我？……等等，你不是打算照我\n"
"做下一个AI吧……\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/3
msgid ""
"Not a bad idea. But I have no intention of ever\n"
"again attempting to transplant\n"
msgstr ""
"主意不坏。但我无意再次\n"
"尝试移植\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/4
msgid ""
"human thought into machines.\n"
msgstr ""
"人类思维移入机器。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/5
msgid ""
"...That's a relief.\n"
msgstr ""
"……放心了。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/6
msgid ""
"You are the man who inherited The Boss's will.\n"
msgstr ""
"你是继承THE BOSS遗志的人。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/7
msgid ""
"You're gathering people around you even now,\n"
msgstr ""
"你到现在还在招兵买马，\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/8
msgid ""
"shaping them, building a new organization. I'd like\n"
"to see how it turns out.\n"
msgstr ""
"塑造他们，组建新组织。我倒想\n"
"看看会变成什么样。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/9
msgid ""
"You're not planning to go back to AI research?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不打算回去做AI研究了？\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/10
msgid ""
"I never said such a thing. Of course my work will\n"
"continue...\n"
msgstr ""
"我可没这么说。我的工作当然会\n"
"继续……\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/11
msgid ""
"Here?\n"
msgstr ""
"在这儿？\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/12
msgid ""
"In my eyes, the growth of MSF\n"
msgstr ""
"在我看来，MSF\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/13
msgid ""
"as an organization is analogous to the development\n"
"of the nervous system.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个组织的成长，就好比神经系统的\n"
"发育。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/14
msgid ""
"The way you become intertwined, stimulate each\n"
"other,\n"
msgstr ""
"你们彼此纠缠、相互刺激，\n"
"彼此，\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/15
msgid ""
"branch out in new directions... It's really quite\n"
"inspirational.\n"
msgstr ""
"再向新方向延伸……真是\n"
"令人深受启发。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/16
msgid ""
"Interesting way to put it.\n"
msgstr ""
"这说法有意思。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/17
msgid ""
"Of course, I intend to repay you for your\n"
"hospitality.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，我会报答你的\n"
"收留之恩。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/18
msgid ""
"The fruits of my research will be at your disposal.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的研究成果随你使用。\n"

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/19
msgid ""
"Why not assign me to the R&D team? I promise you\n"
"won't be disappointed.\n"
msgstr ""
"不如把我编进研发组？我保证\n"
"不会让你失望。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/0
msgid ""
"You know, that ID card I got from Huey wouldn't\n"
"let me into the lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"话说，休伊给我的那张ID卡\n"
"进不了实验室。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/1
msgid ""
"Of course not. I deactivated it.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然不。我注销了。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/3
msgid ""
"As though I'd let him into my lab!\n"
msgstr ""
"我哪会让他进实验室！\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/4
msgid ""
"You don't seem to care for him much. Even though\n"
"you two are in the same field.\n"
msgstr ""
"你好像不太待见他。明明\n"
"你们是同行。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/5
msgid ""
"Oh, please. For starters, I can't stand that\n"
"wishy-washy attitude of his.\n"
msgstr ""
"得了吧。首先，我就受不了他那副\n"
"优柔寡断的样子。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/6
msgid ""
"If he's got something to say to me, he should be a\n"
"man and come say it in person,\n"
msgstr ""
"有话想跟我说，就该像个男人\n"
"当面来讲，\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/7
msgid ""
"not write some furtive letter.\n"
msgstr ""
"而不是写什么密信。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/8
msgid ""
"But if his card doesn't work, how's he supposed to...\n"
msgstr ""
"可他的卡要是不管用，他怎么……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/9
msgid ""
"And another thing! The way he always demeans\n"
"himself.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有！他老是那样\n"
"贬低自己。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/10
msgid ""
"Every other sentence begins with \"I could be\n"
"wrong, but...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"每两句就有一句是“也许我\n"
"错了，但……”\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/11
msgid ""
"Why can't he just do what he does and be\n"
"confident about it?!\n"
msgstr ""
"他就不能干好自己的事，\n"
"有点自信吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/12
msgid ""
"Well, there was the thing about his dissertation\n"
"being plagiarized...\n"
msgstr ""
"说起来，他的论文不是被\n"
"剽窃过吗……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/13
msgid ""
"The real problem is, he doesn't have a whit of\n"
"independence in him.\n"
msgstr ""
"问题是，他\n"
"毫无独立性。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/14
msgid ""
"In Costa Rica, and even back at NASA he was\n"
"always following people around\n"
msgstr ""
"在哥斯达黎加，甚至回NASA后他\n"
"总跟着人转\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/15
msgid ""
"asking if there was some way he could help.\n"
msgstr ""
"问能不能帮上什么忙。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/16
msgid ""
"Why doesn't he stop his whining, take a stand, and\n"
"face up to me?\n"
msgstr ""
"他为什么不停止抱怨，站出来，\n"
"当面跟我讲？\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/17
msgid ""
"I think I know how he feels....\n"
msgstr ""
"我想我懂他的感受……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/18
msgid ""
"And to top it all off, he seems to enjoy referring to\n"
"himself by that nickname I gave him.\n"
msgstr ""
"更糟的是，他似乎很喜欢用我给他起的\n"
"那个绰号称呼自己。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/19
msgid ""
"I simply don't get it. How can he be so submissive?\n"
msgstr ""
"我真不明白。他怎么能这么顺从？\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/20
msgid ""
"So Huey was a nickname you gave him...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以休伊是你给他起的绰号……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/21
msgid ""
"That's right. I took it from the name of a drone in\n"
"the science fiction film \"Silent Running.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。取自科幻片《宇宙静悄悄》里\n"
"一架无人机的名字。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/22
msgid ""
"Drone?\n"
msgstr ""
"无人机？\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/23
msgid ""
"It's a type of worker robot.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种工作机器人。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/24
msgid ""
"The way he follows people, just waiting for them to\n"
"boss him around, is so similar. I couldn't help myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"他跟着人转、等着被使唤的样子太像了。\n"
"我忍不住。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/25
msgid ""
"Oh.. It's an American film directed by Douglas\n"
"Trumbull,\n"
msgstr ""
"哦……那是道格拉斯·特朗布尔执导的\n"
"美国电影，\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/26
msgid ""
"the man who did the special effects for \"2001: A\n"
"Space Odyssey.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"就是给《2001太空漫游》\n"
"做特效的那位。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/27
msgid ""
"Imagine that. A scientist who likes science fiction...\n"
msgstr ""
"真想不到。科学家居然喜欢科幻……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/28
msgid ""
"And that's not all!\n"
msgstr ""
"还不止这些！\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/29
msgid ""
"There's more?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有？\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/30
msgid ""
"He's a man!\n"
msgstr ""
"他是个男人！\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/31
msgid ""
"...Hang on, I seem to remember you saying he\n"
"should be more of a man.\n"
msgstr ""
"……等等，我记得你说过他\n"
"该更有男人样。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/32
msgid ""
"...Yes, well, he is an awfully good scientist.\n"
msgstr ""
"……对，他确实是位出色科学家。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/33
msgid ""
"Without his Reptile Pod, my Mammal Pod wouldn't\n"
"function.\n"
msgstr ""
"没他爬虫舱，我哺乳舱\n"
"就无法运转。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/34
msgid ""
"Just as the cerebrum can't exist without the\n"
"cerebellum and the brain stem.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像没有小脑和脑干，\n"
"大脑就无法存在。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/35
msgid ""
"He did a fine job of designing it, I'll give him that.\n"
msgstr ""
"设计得确实不错，这点我承认。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/36
msgid ""
"That sounded suspiciously like praise...\n"
msgstr ""
"这话听着像是在夸奖……\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/37
msgid ""
"Hmph. It's merely an objective observation.\n"
msgstr ""
"哼。只是客观评价。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/38
msgid ""
"I like people who possess the will to move forward.\n"
msgstr ""
"我喜欢有前进意志的人。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/39
msgid ""
"I have no time for those who refuse to take\n"
"control of their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没时间理会那些不愿掌控\n"
"自己人生的人。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/40
msgid ""
"Until he does, my opinion remains the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那之前，我的看法不变。\n"

#: codec/1/228/0xe4f40/0
msgid ""
"So...you and Cécile seemed to be enjoying\n"
"yourselves back at that lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说……你和塞西尔\n"
"在实验室里似乎很开心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 487..1407
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/0
msgid ""
"Huey's probably mentioned this, but just to be clear,\n"
msgstr ""
"休伊大概提过，但先说清楚，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 1448..2507
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/1
msgid ""
"there's a limit to the parts we can produce here at\n"
"Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们在Mother Base\n"
"零件产量有限。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 2549..4123
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/2
msgid ""
"Therefore, I've built ZEKE's AI using memory boards\n"
"you pulled from other AI weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以，ZEKE的AI用的是从其他AI武器上\n"
"拆下的记忆板。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 4123..4388
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/3
msgid ""
"Will that work?\n"
msgstr ""
"行吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 4402..5726
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/4
msgid ""
"In the human brain, individual functions are spread\n"
"across multiple regions.\n"
msgstr ""
"人脑中，各项功能分散在\n"
"多个区域。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 5767..7746
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/5
msgid ""
"The same is true of AI. Multiple parts sharing the\n"
"same function interlink to strengthen that function.\n"
msgstr ""
"AI也一样。多个部件分担同一功能，\n"
"互相连接来强化该功能。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 7760..8874
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/6
msgid ""
"For example, the more sensor memory boards you\n"
"have,\n"
msgstr ""
"For example, the more sensor memory boards you\n"
"have,\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9975
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/7
msgid ""
"the greater ZEKE's search-and-detect capabilities\n"
"will be.\n"
msgstr ""
"ZEKE的搜索探测能力\n"
"就越强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 10031..11215
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/8
msgid ""
"Install more movement boards and you'll increase\n"
"its mobility.\n"
msgstr ""
"装上更多运动板就能提升\n"
"机动性。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 11215..12496
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/9
msgid ""
"Meaning the AI's capabilities change depending on\n"
"how much memory we give it?\n"
msgstr ""
"也就是说AI的能力取决于\n"
"我们给它多少记忆？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 12510..14113
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/10
msgid ""
"Exactly. The more boards you install, the more\n"
"powerful a function will be.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。装的板越多，\n"
"功能就越强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1239
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/0
msgid ""
"How's the ZEKE AI different from Peace Walker's?\n"
msgstr ""
"ZEKE的AI和和平行者的有何不同？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2452
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/1
msgid ""
"ZEKE's AI isn't a replica of the human thought\n"
"process.\n"
msgstr ""
"ZEKE的AI不是人类思维\n"
"的复制。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3622
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/2
msgid ""
"It isn't programmed to make decisions about\n"
"nuclear retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""
"它没有被编程去做\n"
"核报复决策。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 3775..5126
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/3
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is capable of highly\n"
"independent action in combat\n"
msgstr ""
"但另一方面，它在战斗中能高度\n"
"独立行动，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5126..5879
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/4
msgid ""
"when given orders from a pilot.\n"
msgstr ""
"只要驾驶员下达命令。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5921..7718
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/5
msgid ""
"It can protect infantry, destroy the enemy, and, if\n"
"ordered...\n"
msgstr ""
"它能保护步兵、消灭敌人，如下\n"
"令的话……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7760..8052
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/6
msgid ""
"Launch a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""
"发射核弹\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 8080..8902
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/7
msgid ""
"Let us hope it never comes to that.\n"
msgstr ""
"但愿永远不会到那一步。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 8930..9529
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/8
msgid ""
"My sentiments exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"我完全同意。\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/0
msgid ""
"I'd better fill you in on ZEKE's speech synthesis\n"
"system.\n"
msgstr ""
"我得跟你讲讲\n"
"ZEKE的语音合成系统。\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/1
msgid ""
"Speech synthesis system?\n"
msgstr ""
"语音合成系统？\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/2
msgid ""
"Humans speak for the conventional weapons they\n"
"wield,\n"
msgstr ""
"人类会替自己使用的\n"
"常规武器发声，\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/3
msgid ""
"but an autonomous AI weapon is a different story.\n"
msgstr ""
"但自主AI兵器就不同了。\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/4
msgid ""
"If the AI can't communicate with surrounding\n"
"forces, how can they function as a unit?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果AI无法与周围部队沟通，\n"
"又怎么作为一个单位行动？\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/5
msgid ""
"True. Verbal communication is critical on the\n"
"battlefield.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。战场上\n"
"语言沟通至关重要。\n"

#: codec/1/229/0xe5dd0/6
msgid ""
"Thus, an AI weapon requires a dedicated system to\n"
"produce speech.\n"
msgstr ""
"因此AI兵器需要\n"
"专门的发声系统。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/0
msgid ""
"That was some escape you made from\n"
"Strangelove's lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"你从斯特兰奇洛夫实验室\n"
"逃得真漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/1
msgid ""
"Security inside was not so tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面安保不算严。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/2
msgid ""
"The door to my room was locked from the outside,\n"
"of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"我房间的门从外面锁上了，\n"
"当然是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/3
msgid ""
"But she took off the blindfold at bath time - so she\n"
"could wash my hair...\n"
msgstr ""
"但洗澡时她摘了眼罩，好帮我\n"
"洗头……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/4
msgid ""
"Pretty luxurious treatment for a prisoner.\n"
msgstr ""
"对囚犯来说待遇真奢侈。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/5
msgid ""
"Wasn't it? She wouldn't undo the handcuffs, but\n"
"she washed my body for me instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是吗？她不肯解开手铐，但\n"
"她替我洗了身体。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/6
msgid ""
"And with such gentle care...\n"
msgstr ""
"还那么温柔……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/7
msgid ""
"Why'd you run away? Didn't she say you could go\n"
"home in a month?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为何逃跑？她不是说一个月后\n"
"就能回家吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/8
msgid ""
"If your escape attempt failed, you'd be in greater\n"
"danger than before.\n"
msgstr ""
"逃跑失败，你会比之前\n"
"更危险。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/9
msgid ""
"I was supposed to be giving a presentation\n"
msgstr ""
"我本该去做一场报告，\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/10
msgid ""
"on the distribution of Costa Rican bird species at a\n"
"conference.\n"
msgstr ""
"在会议上，关于哥斯达黎加鸟类的\n"
"分布。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/11
msgid ""
"The date was approaching quickly.\n"
msgstr ""
"日子越来越近了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/12
msgid ""
"So I pretended I had to use the toilet and made\n"
"my escape.\n"
msgstr ""
"于是我假装要上厕所，趁机\n"
"逃跑了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/13
msgid ""
"I found an ID card and searched everywhere for\n"
"my equipment and my tape...\n"
msgstr ""
"我找到张身份证，到处找\n"
"我的装备和磁带……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/14
msgid ""
"But a soldier saw me. It was a miracle I managed\n"
"to get away.\n"
msgstr ""
"但一个士兵看见了我。能\n"
"逃脱真是奇迹。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/15
msgid ""
"There was no time to find the tape.\n"
msgstr ""
"没时间找磁带了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/16
msgid ""
"I don't care about the conference. I'm lucky\n"
"enough to still be in one piece.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不在乎那个会议。我能\n"
"安然无恙就已经很幸运了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/17
msgid ""
"You bounce back quick.\n"
msgstr ""
"你恢复得真快。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/18
msgid ""
"You don't?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/19
msgid ""
"....Not sure. I try not to dwell too much on the past,\n"
"but...\n"
msgstr ""
"……不确定。我尽量不多想过去，\n"
"但……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/20
msgid ""
"Then don't. There's no point. I'm so glad to be out\n"
"of there.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就别想。没意义。我很高兴能离开\n"
"那里。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/21
msgid ""
"I never felt safe, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"我从没觉得安全过，你知道吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/22
msgid ""
"Tell me about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是嘛。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/23
msgid ""
"Well... I think she's interested in women. And I think\n"
"she took a fancy to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……我觉得她对女人感兴趣。而且我觉得\n"
"她看上了我。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/24
msgid ""
"That's, uh.... huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"那，呃…哦。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/25
msgid ""
"Besides, it's much nicer here.\n"
msgstr ""
"再说，这里好多了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/0
msgid ""
"Was it just the two women in the lab?\n"
msgstr ""
"实验室里只有你们两个女人？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/1
msgid ""
"Most of the time, oui.\n"
msgstr ""
"大多数时候，是的。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/2
msgid ""
"Hmm...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/3
msgid ""
"And one of them, you only heard her voice, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"其中一位你只听到了声音，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/4
msgid ""
"Yes, that is correct. Such a wonderful voice. It\n"
"sent chills up my spine.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。那嗓音太美了，\n"
"听得我脊背发凉。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/5
msgid ""
"What was the other woman like?\n"
msgstr ""
"另一位是什么样的人？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/6
msgid ""
"Don't even think about it. She's not the slightest\n"
"interest in men.\n"
msgstr ""
"别打她主意。\n"
"她对男人毫无兴趣。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/7
msgid ""
"No, it's part of my mission to...\n"
msgstr ""
"不，这是我的任务所需……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/8
msgid ""
"Only teasing. Let me think...\n"
msgstr ""
"开个玩笑。让我想想……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/9
msgid ""
"I believe she was in her 30s.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得她三十多岁。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/10
msgid ""
"Pretty, with a good sense of style, but austere in\n"
"her tastes.\n"
msgstr ""
"长得漂亮，品味不错，\n"
"但喜好很朴素。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/11
msgid ""
"A very... Unusual woman.\n"
msgstr ""
"非常……特别的女人。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/12
msgid ""
"And she was doing research on AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"她在做AI研究？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/13
msgid ""
"AI? So that is what she was up to.\n"
msgstr ""
"AI？原来她在做这个。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/0
msgid ""
"Let's go over this one more time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们再过一遍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 1072..2020
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/1
msgid ""
"First, I need an ID card to get into the lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"首先，我得有ID卡才能进实验室。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3385
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/2
msgid ""
"That is correct. From the outside it looks like any\n"
"other ruin.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。从外面看，它就像任何\n"
"其他废墟一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 3427..4778
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/3
msgid ""
"But on the inside it is a state-of-the-art research\n"
"facility.\n"
msgstr ""
"但内部却是一座最先进的研究\n"
"设施。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/4
msgid ""
"And your ID card got taken away from you by\n"
"some guy in an orange jacket.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且你的ID卡被一个穿橙色夹克的\n"
"家伙拿走了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7314
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/5
msgid ""
"Exactly. I heard a quetzal singing nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是。我听到附近有凤尾绿咬鹃在叫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 7453..8164
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/6
msgid ""
"It has not been that long since it happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"事情发生还没过多久。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 8568..10072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/7
msgid ""
"It could be tricky if he's out on patrol, but if he's a\n"
"stationary sentry...\n"
msgstr ""
"他在外巡逻可能有点麻烦，但如果是\n"
"固定哨兵……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10114..10741
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/8
msgid ""
"You don't think the quetzal's moved?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得那只凤尾绿咬鹃没挪窝？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10825..12441
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/9
msgid ""
"Its nest is probably nearby. I do not think it will go\n"
"away anytime soon.\n"
msgstr ""
"它的巢穴大概就在附近。我觉得它不会\n"
"很快离开。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 12483..13318
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/10
msgid ""
"Good. I'll get on looking for that soldier.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我去找那个士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14572
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/11
msgid ""
"If you forget what it sounds like, I'll do the call for\n"
"you again.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你忘了它的叫声，我可以再\n"
"给你演示一遍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 14642..15729
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/12
msgid ""
"Just give me a call anytime you'd like to hear it.\n"
msgstr ""
"想听随时呼我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 16049..16425
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/13
msgid ""
"I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1866
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/0
msgid ""
"Let me get this straight. You were in Costa Rica\n"
"as a birdwatcher?\n"
msgstr ""
"让我理清楚。你在哥斯达黎加\n"
"是作为观鸟者？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3413
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/1
msgid ""
"Yes, I was. Not for pleasure, though - I am a\n"
"researcher, after all.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。不过不是消遣，毕竟我\n"
"是个研究员。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4639
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/2
msgid ""
"I am studying the distribution of Latin American\n"
"bird species.\n"
msgstr ""
"我正在研究拉丁美洲\n"
"鸟类的分布。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5614
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/3
msgid ""
"With today's compact cassette tape recorders,\n"
msgstr ""
"有了如今的紧凑型盒式录音机，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6896
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/4
msgid ""
"even a woman like me can carry her recording\n"
"equipment by herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使像我这样的女人也能独自携带\n"
"录音设备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7077..7843
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/5
msgid ""
"But it was a mistake to come alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"但独自前来是个错误。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7913..9445
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/6
msgid ""
"Mmm. Even so, there sure are a lot of wild birds in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。即便如此，哥斯达黎加的野鸟\n"
"确实很多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 9696..10685
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/7
msgid ""
"Aren't there? Over 800 different species,\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是吗？800多个不同物种，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11925
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/8
#, c-format
msgid ""
"said to be more than 10% of all living bird species\n"
"on Earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说超过地球上所有现存鸟类物种的\n"
"10%。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 12092..13235
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/9
msgid ""
"How many can you name, Mr. Ornithologist?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能叫出多少种，鸟类学家先生？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14349
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/10
msgid ""
"Hey, I was just trying not to scare you...\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，我只是不想吓到你……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 14391..15325
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/11
msgid ""
"You should at least have a basic knowledge of\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"你至少应该对哥斯达黎加有\n"
"基本的了解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 15394..16648
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/12
msgid ""
"How about this: I will give you a thorough\n"
"education,\n"
msgstr ""
"这样吧：我来给你好好\n"
"上一课，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 35876..13513
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/13
msgid ""
"Mr. First-Time Ornithologist.\n"
msgstr ""
"初次观鸟的先生。\n"

#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/14
msgid ""
"Uh, OK. Start by telling me about the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""
"呃，好。先讲讲凤尾绿咬鹃吧。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/0
msgid ""
"Cécile, what's that machine you said you use to\n"
"make those recordings of yours?\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，你说你用来录音的那台机器是\n"
"什么来着？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/1
msgid ""
"A cassette... something or other.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡带……什么的。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/2
msgid ""
"A cassette recorder? Or a cassette densuke, as\n"
"they say in Japon.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡带录音机？还是日本人说的\n"
"卡带densuke？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, that. What is that thing, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""
"对，就那个。那东西到底是啥？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/4
msgid ""
"A portable recording device released last year by a\n"
"Japanese company: Sony.\n"
msgstr ""
"去年日本公司索尼发售的\n"
"便携录音设备。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/5
msgid ""
"It uses compact cassettes, making it far lighter\n"
"than open reel machines.\n"
msgstr ""
"它用紧凑型卡带，比开盘机\n"
"轻得多。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/6
msgid ""
"It still weighs 5 kilograms, but the exercise won't\n"
"kill me!\n"
msgstr ""
"还是有5公斤重，不过这点运动量\n"
"累不死我！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/7
msgid ""
"Ha.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/8
msgid ""
"It's user-friendly, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且很好上手。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/9
msgid ""
"All the buttons have markings on them,\n"
msgstr ""
"所有按键上都有标记，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/10
msgid ""
"allowing you to operate it without looking at it.\n"
msgstr ""
"不用看也能操作。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/11
msgid ""
"Can you imagine missing the shot of a lifetime\n"
"simply because you'd blinked?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能想象就因为眨了下眼\n"
"错过一生一次的镜头吗？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/12
msgid ""
"That would be devastating.\n"
msgstr ""
"那太要命了。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/13
msgid ""
"But where'd they come up with densuke? It sounds\n"
"like a Japanese name.\n"
msgstr ""
"可densuke这名字哪来的？听着\n"
"像日本名。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/14
msgid ""
"Allow me to field that one.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个我来答。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/15
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/6
msgid ""
"Kaz?!\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹？！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/16
msgid ""
"Densuke's a nickname that comes from the name\n"
"of an old manga character.\n"
msgstr ""
"densuke是绰号，来自一部老漫画\n"
"角色的名字。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/17
msgid ""
"Was he some recording nerd, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"他也是个录音宅？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/18
msgid ""
"Don't gimme that! Recording atmospheric noises is\n"
"an exhilarating art!\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么说！录环境音可是\n"
"一门刺激的艺术！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/19
msgid ""
"There's nothing like capturing the real world in\n"
"action on tape!\n"
msgstr ""
"把真实世界录进磁带里的感觉\n"
"无可替代！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/20
msgid ""
"It's just like taking pictures with a camera,\n"
msgstr ""
"就跟用镜头拍照一样，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/21
msgid ""
"only with a microphone instead of a viewfinder.\n"
msgstr ""
"只不过用麦克风代替取景器。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/22
msgid ""
"Sure...\n"
msgstr ""
"当然\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/23
msgid ""
"Listen to a tape with your eyes closed\n"
msgstr ""
"闭上眼听磁带\n"
